  "content": {
    "id": "p8-q38-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": null,
    "prompt": "The polynomial $x^4-4x^3+ax^2-4x+3$ is divided by $x^2+1$.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p8-q38-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "Find the quotient and remainder in terms of $a$.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$Q(x)=x^2-4x+a-1$, $R(x)=4-a$.",
          "worked": "Successive subtraction gives\n$$\\begin{align*}\nx^4-4x^3+ax^2-4x+3-x^2(x^2+1)&=-4x^3+(a-1)x^2-4x+3\\\\\n-4x^3+(a-1)x^2-4x+3-(-4x)(x^2+1)&=(a-1)x^2+3\\\\\n(a-1)x^2+3-(a-1)(x^2+1)&=4-a.\n\\end{align*}$$\nHence\n$$x^4-4x^3+ax^2-4x+3=(x^2+1)(x^2-4x+a-1)+(4-a).$$\nThe quotient is $Q(x)=x^2-4x+a-1$ and the remainder is $R(x)=4-a$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 60
      },
      {
        "id": "p8-q38-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "Find the value of $a$ if $x^2+1$ is a factor of the polynomial.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$a=4$.",
          "worked": "A factor gives remainder zero.\n$$\\begin{align*}\n4-a&=0\\\\\na&=4.\n\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 28
      }
    ]
  },
